{{ElectionsNE}}
The '''1994 Nebraska United States Senate election''' was held on November 8, 1994. Incumbent Democratic Senator [[Bob Kerrey]] ran for re-election to a second term. He was challenged in the general election by Republican nominee Jan Stoney, a retired telecommunications executive. Despite [[1994 United States elections|nationwide Republican gains]], Kerrey won re-election by a comfortable margin.

